    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nThis exceptional site off Stoney Boreen, Myrtleville, Co. Cork presents a rare opportunity to acquire a superb coastal property in one of Cork's most desirable seaside locations. Extending to approximately 0.49 acres, the site enjoys magnificent sea views stretching beyond the beautiful sands of Myrtleville Beach, offering a stunning natural backdrop and an enviable setting for a future home.\nIdeally positioned within the residential development boundary area, the site benefits from strong development potential, with no known restrictions on planning, making it an attractive proposition for private home buyers or those seeking to build a bespoke coastal residence. Its elevated position not only enhances the views but also adds to the overall sense of privacy and exclusivity.\nThe location is equally impressive. The beach is just a short stroll away, along with a selection of popular bars, restaurants, cafés, and local shops, all within comfortable walking distance, creating a vibrant yet relaxed coastal lifestyle. Myrtleville is renowned for its community atmosphere, scenic walks, and year-round appeal.\nCrosshaven village is only a five-minute drive, providing further amenities, schools, marinas, and services, while Cork City remains easily accessible, making this an ideal balance of coastal living and convenience.\nThis is a rare and highly desirable site combining outstanding sea views, prime location, and excellent development potential—an opportunity not to be missed in one of Cork's most sought-after coastal settings."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Negotiator",
        "SortOrder": 10,
        "Content": "Trevor O'Sullivan"
      }
